cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Every use authorized by LICENSE requires full citation of the paper and of this repository when its files are used, including media and internal use; see LICENSE Section 6 for citation content and placement."
type: dataset
title: "The Primitive Recursor Test: Sessions, Reader Records, Scoring Programs, and Reference Proofs"
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
abstract: >
  Prompts, model sessions, reader records, scoring programs, scored tables,
  and Lean and TTT2 evidence for the paper "The Primitive Recursor Test":
  30 language models, 4,160 sessions and 18 test surfaces on the termination
  proof for the step-duplicating primitive recursor
  F(x,y,Z) -> x, F(x,y,S(n)) -> G(y,F(x,y,n)). Sessions are scored on the
  termination verdict, the mathematical validity of the proof, and whether
  the proof is derived from the displayed rules, against answers fixed by
  TTT2 and CeTA certificates and Lean 4 theorems.
